          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            When regarding a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            defined by how it is probed by test spaces (cf.
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+geometry"} functorial geometry
            %em concrete sheaf
            is a generalized space that has an
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of points
            out of which it is built.
          %p
            So a concrete sheaf models a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            that is given by a set of points and a choice of which morphisms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            from concrete test spaces into it count as “structure preserving” (e.g. count as smooth, when the sheaf models a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth space
          %p
            More in the intrinsic language of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            %em concrete sheaf
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+site"} concrete site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            that, while perhaps not
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            of a sheaf of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ,
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U \mapsto Hom_{Set}(|U|, S)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |U|
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |U| \coloneqq Hom_C({*}, U)
            of points underlying the object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+site"} concrete site
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            For the category of concrete sheaves
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Conc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Conc(Sh(C))
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+sections"} global sections
            functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
